>>so, my question is, what is the worthless gems good for anyway?!?!?!?!?!

>...throw them at co-aligned unicorns (ie. a black unicorn if you are a
>chaotic character).  If the unicorn "graciously accepts your gift," then
>your luck will likely increase (someone who knows the source code like the
>back of their hand will know the exact percentage--Peter?).

The chance is 0.

If the gem is identified as worthless glass the unicorn won't
accept it.

The chance is also 0 if the unicorn is tame (a pet).

Otherwise the chance is 100%.

If the gem was unidentified, the luck increases by 1.
If it is a real gem and a co-aligned unicorn, it increases 5.
If it is a real gem and a non-aligned unicorn, it increases by rn2(7)-3.

Any gem (identified or not) make any unicorn peaceful.
